 r"I am writing to apply for the Graduate Data \& AI Engineer position at Altrad, based in Middlesbrough or Goldthorpe. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK.",

 r"What attracts me to this role is that it is about making AI useful inside a large, practical business: building agents and retrieval tools that help employees find information and automate routine work, and testing them carefully so that people can trust the answers. That is the kind of work I have enjoyed most so far.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked on a patient-facing AI assistant for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses using LLM-as-judge prompts, and I designed a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric with red-line rules to test answers for accuracy and unsafe content. The client adopted the benchmark and rubric as its acceptance standard. I also helped build a medically reviewed knowledge graph, ran blinded A/B tests of its effect on answer quality, and built a regex and LLM extraction pipeline that turned more than 4,800 free-text consultation threads into structured data.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build KPI frameworks and dashboards for operations, product and commercial teams. I also used Claude Code to build an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of our analytics workflow, with a validation step to check its outputs, and it is now used by my own team and by adjacent teams. Outside work I have built a retrieval-augmented question-answering agent over NHS health content, combining keyword and embedding search with a guardrail for red-flag symptoms.",

 r"I should be clear about some gaps. I have used Power BI, but I have not yet worked with Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Factory, Databricks or Copilot Studio, and my data engineering experience comes from analysis pipelines rather than building a lakehouse. These are the tools I would be keen to learn in this role.",

 r"I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029, after which I would need sponsorship. I am based in London and happy to relocate to Middlesbrough or Goldthorpe. Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to Altrad's data and AI work.",
